.\"
.\" Manual page of "mcp-python-chart" - the launcher of the MCP server
.\" "mcp-python" by its Helm chart, in a K3s cluster of the current user.
.\" The secrets, the common environment and the security of the server -
.\" in "mcp-python-container.1".
.\"
.\" View the source: man ./chart/mcp-python-chart.1
.TH MCP-PYTHON-CHART 1 2026-11-15 "mcp-python-chart" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-python-chart \- the MCP server mcp-python of the current user, by its Helm chart, in K3s
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-python-chart
.RB [ \-\-chart
.IR TGZ | DIR ]
.B up
.RI [ "helm upgrade options" ]
.br
.B mcp-python-chart
.BR status " | " logs " | " test " | " down
.br
.B mcp-python-chart
.BR kubectl " | " helm
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B mcp-python-chart
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-python-chart
deploys the
.BR mcp-python (8)
server - an MCP server, which runs a Python 3 code for its clients - by
its Helm chart, into a K3s cluster of the user who runs it. The cluster is
a container of the local Docker, made by the launcher, and runs in the
background, back after a restart of Docker or of the host. No image
registry and no chart repository are needed. The same server without
Kubernetes -
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
.BR mcp-python-compose (1).
.PP
HTTPS by the Ingress (Traefik of K3s) at port
.B 8443
.RB ( MCP_INGRESS_PORT ),
published at
.B 127.0.0.1
of the host
.RB ( MCP_PUBLISH_HOST ),
for the host names of the TLS certificate.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B up
Makes the secrets and loads the image, as
.BR mcp-python-container (1)
describes; makes the cluster, or starts it again; loads the image into the
cluster; applies the certificate and the token files as Secrets; installs
or upgrades the release and waits for it. More arguments go to
.BR "helm upgrade" ,
e.g.
.BR "\-\-set config.execTimeout=120" .
Run again - the Secrets are applied again: a client added or removed is
noticed by the server in about a minute, no restart.
.TP
.B status
The state of the cluster, the pods, the service and the Ingress.
.TP
.B logs
The log of the server, until Ctrl C.
.TP
.B test
.B helm test
of the release - the listener accepts connections.
.TP
.B down
The cluster removed, with all its state. The secrets of the user stay.
.TP
.BR kubectl ", " helm
The tool at the cluster of the user, with the arguments. The same, with
no launcher - the kubeconfig of the cluster in
.BR KUBECONFIG :
.RS
.PP
.EX
export KUBECONFIG=~/.local/share/mcp-python/k3s/kubeconfig.yaml
kubectl \-\-namespace mcp-python get pods
helm \-\-namespace mcp-python list
.EE
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-chart " \fITGZ\fR|\fIDIR\fR"
The chart - a packed one or a directory. Default - the chart of the
package
.RB ( MCP_CHART ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/mcp-python-chart/mcp-python-server-<version>.tgz
The chart.
.TP
.I /usr/share/mcp-python-chart/mcp-python-chart-values.yaml
The values of the release - the loaded image, the Secrets, the Ingress.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mcp-python/k3s/kubeconfig.yaml
The kubeconfig of the cluster, mode 0600 - the credentials of its
administrator. Used by the commands
.B kubectl
and
.BR helm .
.PP
The secrets of the user - see
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
FILES.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B KUBECONFIG
is set by the launcher, whatever the environment has - the commands are
always at the cluster of the user. The rest - the same as of
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
besides
.BR CONTAINER_TOOL :
the cluster is a container of Docker only. And:
.TP
.B MCP_CHART
The chart, as
.BR \-\-chart .
.TP
.B MCP_INGRESS_PORT
The host port of the Ingress. Default
.BR 8443 .
.TP
.B MCP_K3S_API_PORT
The host port of the Kubernetes API, at
.B 127.0.0.1
only. Default
.BR 16443 .
.TP
.B MCP_K3S_IMAGE
The image of K3s.
.SH SECURITY
The K3s container is privileged - it has full access to the host while it
runs.
.PP
In the cluster the server runs as its own account. The token files are a
Secret mounted into the pod, readable by that account - they keep the
SHA-256 of the tokens, not the tokens. The certificate and its key are
used by Traefik only; the pod serves plain HTTP within the cluster.
.SH EXAMPLES
The server, and a check of it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mcp-python-chart up
mcp-python-chart test
.EE
.RE
.PP
One more client - its token in
.IR ~/.local/share/mcp-python/clients/laptop.token :
.PP
.RS
.EX
MCP_CLIENT=laptop mcp-python-chart up
.EE
.RE
.PP
Another chart, unpacked:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mcp-python-chart \-\-chart ./mcp-python-server up
.EE
.RE
.PP
The server by hand, then back to the shell:
.PP
.RS
.EX
export KUBECONFIG=~/.local/share/mcp-python/k3s/kubeconfig.yaml
kubectl \-\-namespace mcp-python rollout restart deployment
kubectl \-\-namespace mcp-python port\-forward service/mcp\-python\-mcp\-python\-server 8765
unset KUBECONFIG
.EE
.RE
.PP
All gone:
.PP
.RS
.EX
mcp-python-chart down
.EE
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.BR docker ,
.B kubectl
and
.B helm
at the host.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcp-python-container (1),
.BR mcp-python-compose (1),
.BR mcp-python (8),
.BR helm (1),
.BR kubectl (1)
